<!--
  Slide 09 — Flow Metrics Snapshot (metrics 1-7)
  Type: content-slide
  Required tokens (substituted by render_deck.py from metrics.json):
    {{M1_DISPLAY}}, {{M1_CONF}}, {{M1_CONF_LABEL}}, {{M1_CAVEAT}}   Flow Load
    {{M2_DISPLAY}}, {{M2_CONF}}, {{M2_CONF_LABEL}}, {{M2_CAVEAT}}   Flow Velocity
    {{M3_DISPLAY}}, {{M3_CONF}}, {{M3_CONF_LABEL}}, {{M3_CAVEAT}}   Flow Predictability
    {{M4_DISPLAY}}, {{M4_CONF}}, {{M4_CONF_LABEL}}, {{M4_CAVEAT}}   Flow Active
    {{M5_DISPLAY}}, {{M5_CONF}}, {{M5_CONF_LABEL}}, {{M5_CAVEAT}}   Flow Efficiency
    {{M6_DISPLAY}}, {{M6_CONF}}, {{M6_CONF_LABEL}}, {{M6_CAVEAT}}   Flow Distribution
                                                                    (point-difference string,
                                                                    no trailing × — see
                                                                    Rendering notes)
    {{M7_DISPLAY}}, {{M7_CONF}}, {{M7_CONF_LABEL}}, {{M7_CAVEAT}}   Flow Time
  Required non-text visual: <table class="metric-table"> (satisfies Rule 5
  content-slide visual requirement; theme.css §Phase 9 styles this table).

  Authority: AAP §0.4.1 (file inventory enumerates this filename),
  §0.2.2 (Metrics 1-7 align with the Flow Framework — Flow Load,
  Velocity, Predictability, Active, Efficiency, Distribution, Time),
  §0.7.1 Rule 5 (content-slide constraints — max 4 bullets, ≤40 body
  words, ≥1 non-text visual, zero emoji, no fenced code blocks),
  §0.7.2.1 (canonical phrasing "Insufficient signal — [reason]" when
  data is lacking; MUST NOT fabricate or extrapolate), §0.7.2.2 Rule 3
  (Confidence Transparency — every derived metric carries a tag AND
  every Low / Insufficient-signal metric carries an explicit caveat;
  satisfied by the per-row Caveat column below), §0.7.2.2 Rule 4
  (Internal Consistency — values here must match acceleration-report.md,
  Traceability Matrix, and Acceleration Curve).

  Rendering notes:
    - This template is consumed by render_deck.py, which substitutes the
      twenty-eight tokens above from metrics.json and writes the result
      into acceleration/executive-presentation.html.
    - Each *_DISPLAY token is a renderer-pre-formatted string. For a
      numeric multiplier (e.g., "3.2") the renderer appends the Unicode
      multiplier sign U+00D7 (MULTIPLICATION SIGN), NOT the ASCII letter
      x (U+0078). For a non-numeric value the renderer substitutes the
      canonical phrase "Insufficient signal — <reason>" verbatim with
      NO trailing × — the hardcoded suffix anti-pattern is avoided by
      construction so an unmeasurable metric never renders as
      "Insufficient signal — <reason>×". The "Insufficient signal"
      phrasing is canonical per AAP §0.7.2.1 and MUST NOT be replaced
      by alternative wordings such as "unavailable" or "missing".
    - Metric 6 (Flow Distribution) is a work-type mix and is reported
      as a point-difference string (for example, a delta-prefixed list
      of conventional-commit prefix shifts) or "see Deep-Dive 6", not
      a single scalar multiplier. The renderer therefore emits
      {{M6_DISPLAY}} without any × suffix regardless of the underlying
      value's shape.
    - Each *_CAVEAT token expands to the canonical caveat string from
      metrics.json (per AAP §0.7.2.2 Rule 3 — every Low or
      Insufficient-signal metric MUST carry an explicit caveat). When
      a metric is High-confidence with no caveat to surface, the
      renderer substitutes the empty string and the cell renders blank.
      Sourced from metrics.json:"metrics.<name>.caveat".
    - Each *_CONF token expands to the CSS class suffix
      ("high" | "medium" | "low"), so the rendered span becomes
      <span class="confidence-low">Low</span>. The confidence badge
      styles are defined in acceleration/templates/deck/theme.css
      (.confidence-high / .confidence-medium / .confidence-low).
    - Per the AAP Confidence Rubric (§0.8.3): a metric derived from
      direct issue-tracker counts is High; a metric approximated from
      git commit patterns is Medium; a metric inferred from indirect
      proxies is Low. Confidence is assigned by the extractor at
      runtime based on the actual data source used — the template only
      surfaces the resolved class and label.
    - The renderer is the single source of truth (metrics.json); the
      multipliers shown here MUST be identical to the values reported
      in acceleration-report.md (Rule 4 — Internal Consistency,
      verified by verify_report.py which parses both the rendered
      Markdown and this rendered HTML and asserts equality).
    - Tone discipline (Rule 2 — Factual-Neutral): the metric labels
      are the canonical Flow Framework names — the forbidden
      subjective-qualifier list in the Boundaries directive does not
      appear in the visible slide body.
    - Body word count outside the <table>: "Flow Framework" +
      "Flow Metrics (1–7)" = 5 words, well under the Rule 5 cap of 40.
-->
<section class="content-slide">
  <span class="eyebrow">Flow Framework</span>
  <h3>Flow Metrics (1–7)</h3>
  <table class="metric-table">
    <colgroup>
      <col class="col-index">
      <col class="col-metric">
      <col class="col-value">
      <col class="col-conf">
      <col class="col-caveat">
    </colgroup>
    <thead>
      <tr><th>#</th><th>Metric</th><th>Multiplier</th><th>Confidence</th><th>Caveat</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>1</td><td>Flow Load</td><td>{{M1_DISPLAY}}</td><td><span class="confidence-{{M1_CONF}}">{{M1_CONF_LABEL}}</span></td><td>{{M1_CAVEAT}}</td></tr>
      <tr><td>2</td><td>Flow Velocity</td><td>{{M2_DISPLAY}}</td><td><span class="confidence-{{M2_CONF}}">{{M2_CONF_LABEL}}</span></td><td>{{M2_CAVEAT}}</td></tr>
      <tr><td>3</td><td>Flow Predictability</td><td>{{M3_DISPLAY}}</td><td><span class="confidence-{{M3_CONF}}">{{M3_CONF_LABEL}}</span></td><td>{{M3_CAVEAT}}</td></tr>
      <tr><td>4</td><td>Flow Active</td><td>{{M4_DISPLAY}}</td><td><span class="confidence-{{M4_CONF}}">{{M4_CONF_LABEL}}</span></td><td>{{M4_CAVEAT}}</td></tr>
      <tr><td>5</td><td>Flow Efficiency</td><td>{{M5_DISPLAY}}</td><td><span class="confidence-{{M5_CONF}}">{{M5_CONF_LABEL}}</span></td><td>{{M5_CAVEAT}}</td></tr>
      <tr><td>6</td><td>Flow Distribution</td><td>{{M6_DISPLAY}}</td><td><span class="confidence-{{M6_CONF}}">{{M6_CONF_LABEL}}</span></td><td>{{M6_CAVEAT}}</td></tr>
      <tr><td>7</td><td>Flow Time</td><td>{{M7_DISPLAY}}</td><td><span class="confidence-{{M7_CONF}}">{{M7_CONF_LABEL}}</span></td><td>{{M7_CAVEAT}}</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
</section>
